WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.160
Origin stories, Amazons, and&nbsp;
Nicolas Cage — there's a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.460
of things we'll never see from&nbsp;
these DC shows that got the ax.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.860
In the live-action world, DC hasn't had a lot&nbsp;
of luck with the Green Lantern. First off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:19.500
the film starring Ryan Reynolds, which was meant&nbsp;
to kickstart the DCEU, flopped at the box office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:25.800
making $219 million from a $200 million budget.&nbsp;
Then, the attempt to introduce the hero in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:32.640
Arrowverse was largely a start-stop affair, as The&nbsp;
CW never fully unleashed John Diggle as the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.440
Green Lantern. There seemed to be some hope on the&nbsp;
horizon, though, as the Arrowverse's mastermind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.720
Greg Berlanti, began work on a "Green&nbsp;
Lantern" TV series for HBO Max in 2019.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.640
Berlanti brought in Seth Grahame-Smith as a&nbsp;
writer and showrunner for the series. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.600
Grahame-Smith is no novice to comic book&nbsp;
adaptations, having written the story for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.560
"The Lego Batman Movie." The showrunner got&nbsp;
to work on the "Green Lantern" show, and two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.480
leads were cast in the shape of Finn Wittrock&nbsp;
as Guy Gardner and Jeremy Irvine as Alan Scott.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.820
The show would have featured other Lanterns from&nbsp;
the comics, as well as an entirely new Lantern.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:10.260
Grahame-Smith completed eight episodes&nbsp;
for the first season. In October 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.020
however, a decision was made to&nbsp;
pivot in a different direction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:17.280
and make the show about John Stewart. The&nbsp;
showrunner departed the show thereafter.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.280
The launch of HBO Max ushered in a wave of&nbsp;
excitement from DC fans. As Warner Bros.'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.260
official streaming service, part of the grand&nbsp;
plan was to utilize DC's properties to create&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:33.720
exclusive shows for the platform. In 2021, Variety&nbsp;
reported that a "Constantine" series was being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:38.160
developed by J. J. Abrams and his Bad Robot&nbsp;
Productions company. Reportedly, it would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:43.620
formed a part of the "Justice League Dark" world&nbsp;
that Abrams was set to build out for HBO Max.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:47.340
There were also rumors floating around&nbsp;
social media that "Gangs of London" star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.120
Ṣọpẹ́ Dìrísù was in line to portray&nbsp;
the Hellblazer on the show. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.540
the actor told NME that he wasn't&nbsp;
ever going to play Constantine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:58.860
though stopped short of discussing if he had&nbsp;
been cast for another role in the series.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:02.400
In September 2022, something&nbsp;
that no one expected happened:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.140
a sequel to the 2005 "Constantine" film&nbsp;
was announced. According to Variety,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.820
Keanu Reeves would return to portray the lead&nbsp;
character on the big screen. Simultaneously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:15.960
the film's announcement also signaled the&nbsp;
end for HBO Max's "Constantine" series.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.880
"A gift, John."

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:24.120
One of the more interesting propositions that&nbsp;
was meant to debut on the DC Universe streaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:29.040
app was a show called "Metropolis." The drama&nbsp;
series was meant to act as a Superman prequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:33.840
that would have followed Lex Luthor and Lois Lane&nbsp;
in the infamous city as they explored the mythos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:39.840
of this part of the DC Universe. The brains behind&nbsp;
"Metropolis" were John Stephens and Danny Cannon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.560
who had been the executive producers&nbsp;
on the Fox series "Gotham." Thirteen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.300
episodes were ordered in 2018, with plans&nbsp;
for the show to air in 2019. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.420
Deadline later reported that the&nbsp;
show went into redevelopment.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.440
Later that year, though, The Hollywood&nbsp;
Reporter confirmed the show had been canned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.540
despite no official announcement from DC about&nbsp;
the project's status. That said, it's safe to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:05.040
say that whichever incarnation of the series&nbsp;
was planned back then is all but dead in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.900
water now. Perhaps some of the ideas for the show&nbsp;
might be utilized for future Superman adaptations.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:16.860
Having debuted in "Omega Men" #3, it took Lobo&nbsp;
36 years to make his live-action debut in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:21.780
second season of the SyFy series "Krypton."&nbsp;
The Main Man is portrayed by Emmett J. Scanlan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:26.700
who embraced the character's wild nature&nbsp;
and won over many fans who had doubted his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:31.380
casting at first. However, Lobo's appearance&nbsp;
in "Krypton" was meant to serve as a backdoor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:36.300
pilot for his own show. Scanlan had signed&nbsp;
on to star in his own solo series, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:40.380
would have featured "Krypton" executive producer&nbsp;
Cameron Welsh being involved in the spinoff too.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.880
Unfortunately, the ratings for Season 2&nbsp;
dropped dramatically, and "Krypton" was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:49.140
canceled. The "Lobo" TV series ended up being&nbsp;
collateral damage in the process as well.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:54.000
In an interview with CBR, Scanlan reflected&nbsp;
on playing Lobo, saying the character was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.380
the perfect merger of Wolverine and The&nbsp;
Joker. He added how thinking about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:04.260
Main Man brings back fond memories; however, he is&nbsp;
disappointed that his run ended so unexpectedly.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:10.560
"Holy fragaroli! F-f-f-feels&nbsp;
like I'm being torn apart! Cool."

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:16.680
"Arrow" birthed a number of other shows,&nbsp;
such as "The Flash" and "DC's Legends of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.700
Tomorrow." The Season 8 episode titled&nbsp;
"Green Arrow &amp; The Canaries" was meant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:24.900
to serve as a backdoor pilot for a future&nbsp;
spinoff series of the same name on The CW.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:29.760
The storyline was set in 2040 where Oliver&nbsp;
Queen's daughter, Mia, takes up the Green&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:34.740
Arrow mantle and teams up with Laurel Lance&nbsp;
and Dinah Drake to take down the rogues.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:39.360
In January 2021, the plug was pulled&nbsp;
on any potential "Green Arrow &amp; The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.020
Canaries" series as The CW decided&nbsp;
not to go ahead with it. Soon after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:46.080
"Arrow" co-creator Marc Guggenheim&nbsp;
revealed on Twitter that the decision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:49.560
was largely influenced by the&nbsp;
effects of the COVID-19 pandemic.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.640
Katie Cassidy wasn't too shattered by this&nbsp;
turn of events, though, as she explained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.960
to ComicBookMovie.com that the Arrowverse&nbsp;
had been more than successful. She said:
 &nbsp;

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.960
"I say this in the most respectful, kind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.160
realistic way ... We really,&nbsp;
really milked that cow."

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:08.100
"I don't think I've taken down&nbsp;
so many buildings at once."

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:13.920
There's a reason the "Titans" TV series doesn't&nbsp;
have "teen" anywhere in its title. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.700
there are many "Teen Titans" fans&nbsp;
who would love nothing more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:21.660
to see a live-action adaptation of&nbsp;
the beloved, youthful team and all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.920
their exuberance. And it almost happened&nbsp;
before "Titans" received the green light.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:29.820
As reported by Variety, TNT had&nbsp;
planned to make a "Teen Titans"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:34.680
show that centered around Dick Grayson and his&nbsp;
transition from Robin to Nightwing. In 2016,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:39.780
former TNT president Kevin Reilly announced the&nbsp;
production had been shelved and would not take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:45.480
flight at all. The Titans lived on, though,&nbsp;
and finally received their own show in 2018.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:51.540
The CW's Arrowverse proved that it wasn't afraid&nbsp;
to take risks on relatively newer DC characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:56.820
like Naomi. In fact, there was even a plan to&nbsp;
create a "Wonder Girl" show about Yara Flor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:01.740
the hero who is half-Amazonian and&nbsp;
half-Brazilian rain god. Flor hadn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:05.700
even made her debut in DC Comics at&nbsp;
the time of this announcement in 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:09.300
but she had been deemed compelling and&nbsp;
interesting enough to get her own show.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.600
Unfortunately, it felt like the brakes&nbsp;
were pumped on the series before it had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:17.280
even gotten out of first gear. Co-showrunner&nbsp;
and writer Dailyn Rodriguez broke the news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:21.180
about the cancellation of "Wonder Girl"&nbsp;
on her Twitter account in February 2021.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.780
Yara Flor went on to make her&nbsp;
official debut in "Dark Nights:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:28.260
Death Metal" #7, which was&nbsp;
released in January 2021.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:33.840
For three seasons, Hawk and Dove were an&nbsp;
important part of "Titans" as everyone's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:37.200
favorite crime-fighting couple. After&nbsp;
Jason Todd clipped Hawk's wings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:42.000
Dove also fluttered away from the series. Actor&nbsp;
Alan Ritchson revealed to Entertainment Weekly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.420
that it wasn't his decision to leave&nbsp;
the show, but a choice made by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.960
creative team and producers who needed&nbsp;
to cut down the number of cast members.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:53.880
Discussing his experience on "Titans," Ritchson&nbsp;
shared some important details about the characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:58.620
of Hawk and Dove, and how they were originally&nbsp;
supposed to feature from the inception. He said:

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:03.360
"My initial deal was for two episodes,&nbsp;
and I had a separate deal for a Hawk and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:07.920
Dove spin-off. And when we shot those two&nbsp;
episodes, they really enjoyed us as Titans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:11.820
and invited us to join more episodes&nbsp;
in the back half of the first season."

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:16.200
Ritchson added he believed the chances&nbsp;
of a spinoff were always unlikely if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.680
the characters were a core part of the&nbsp;
Titans team, but he was told that it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:24.420
happen since they were so popular on the show.&nbsp;
Unfortunately, the spinoff never materialized.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.460
"You didn't wait for me."

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:27.600
"You would have said not tonight."

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:34.080
The superhero Static first captured the public's&nbsp;
attention with the release of the "Static Shock"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:40.020
animated show. Running for 52 episodes, fans&nbsp;
fell in love with Virgil Hawkins and how he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:44.880
balanced the crime-fighting life with the trials&nbsp;
and tribulations of being a teenager. The goodwill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:49.740
of the series resulted in many people wondering&nbsp;
when a live-action version of Static would debut.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:54.180
In 2014, Warner Bros. unveiled a new&nbsp;
division called Blue Ribbon Content,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:59.580
which would be responsible for creating shows and&nbsp;
cartoons for the studio. One of the first projects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:04.860
announced for this venture was a live-action&nbsp;
"Static Shock" show created by director, writer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:09.480
and producer Reginald Hudlin. A year later, in&nbsp;
an interview with Flicks and the City, actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:14.280
Tyler James Williams suggested that Jaden Smith&nbsp;
had already been cast as the lead for the show.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:19.620
As interesting as the show sounded, it never&nbsp;
seemed to go anywhere. The idea for the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:24.480
appears to have morphed into a film, as it&nbsp;
was announced in March 2021 that Hudlin and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:27.960
Michael B. Jordan would be producing&nbsp;
a live-action "Static Shock" movie.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:33.900
The superhero boom in the 2010s inspired&nbsp;
networks and studios to get in on a piece of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:39.000
the action. Considering the success of the '70s&nbsp;
"Wonder Woman" TV series starring Lynda Carter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.720
executives must have been salivating at&nbsp;
the thought of trying something similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:47.940
in a more lucrative, modern era. In 2011, a&nbsp;
pilot for a new potential show was produced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:52.620
which starred Adrianne Palicki as the titular&nbsp;
hero — but it was never picked up. A year later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:56.520
Vulture reported that The CW was eyeing&nbsp;
a series that would follow a young Diana&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.520 --> 00:09:00.660
Prince before she became Wonder Woman. The&nbsp;
working title for the show was "Amazon."

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:05.880
For a few years, murmurs about the project&nbsp;
occasionally popped up, and the show remained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:10.320
a possibility. However, it all went ice-cold&nbsp;
after the confirmation that Gal Gadot would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:16.380
portray Wonder Woman in the DC Extended Universe.&nbsp;
The CW's former CEO Mark Pedowitz revealed at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:21.300
2017 TV Critics' Association that the network&nbsp;
ceased all plans to take a stab at "Amazon"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:25.740
after the success of Gadot's Wonder Woman&nbsp;
had ended any chance of it ever happening.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.480
"You are stronger than you believe."

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:32.940
August 2022 was a tumultuous time for DC fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:37.080
as the new leadership of Warner Bros.&nbsp;
Discovery took the hammer to various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:41.580
projects. It all started with the shocking&nbsp;
cancellation of the "Batgirl" movie, but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:46.560
anthology series "Strange Adventures" was also&nbsp;
revealed to be off the table around this time.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:51.000
However, the news of the show's cancellation&nbsp;
was actually broken by filmmaker Kevin Smith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:54.900
on his podcast "Hollywood Babble-On."&nbsp;
Smith explained he had been working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:59.400
on an episode for the show that would have&nbsp;
featured Bizarro and Jimmy Olsen. He added&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:02.820
that he was trying to secure Nicolas&nbsp;
Cage's services to portray Bizarro,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:07.200
which would have certainly been a big get for&nbsp;
the production. The Hollywood Reporter cited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:12.960
its own sources that said the project had been&nbsp;
silently canned months before the WB-DC purge.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:19.380
In the world of comics, Madame Xanadu is a&nbsp;
well-known and powerful sorcerer in the mystic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:23.880
part of the DC Universe. It might have taken a&nbsp;
while to happen, but the character eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:29.340
made her live-action debut in 2019's "Swamp Thing"&nbsp;
TV show, where she was portrayed by actor Jeryl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:33.540
Prescott. While it would have made sense to&nbsp;
spin off the character from that series into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:39.510
her own solo vehicle, the controversial axing of&nbsp;
"Swamp Thing" ended this iteration of Madame X.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:44.400
However, J. J. Abrams and his production&nbsp;
company, Bad Robot, had other ideas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:49.140
which would have incorporated Madame X&nbsp;
into their vision of DC shows on HBO Max.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:54.180
Abrams' end goal was to create a "Justice&nbsp;
League Dark" franchise for the streamer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:58.920
in which multiple characters would have had&nbsp;
their own programs. One part of the overall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:03.720
puzzle was a "Madame X" series that would have&nbsp;
been helmed by writer, director, and producer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:08.700
Angela Robinson. Unfortunately, the turbulence&nbsp;
at Warner Bros. Discovery and its upheaval of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:13.920
DC programming in 2022 claimed yet another&nbsp;
victim in the shape of the "Madame X" show.

